                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+deformation+quantization"} strict deformation quantization
          %h2#references References
          %p The concept of formal deformation quantization originates with:
          %ul
            %li#BayenFlatoFronsdalLichnerowiczSternheimer78
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fran%C3%A7ois+Bayen"}> François Bayen
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mosh%C3%A9+Flato"} Moshé Flato
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christian+Fronsdal"} Christian Fronsdal
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andr%C3%A9+Lichnerowicz"} André Lichnerowicz
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Sternheimer"} Daniel Sternheimer
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Deformation theory and quantization. I. Deformations of symplectic structures.
                %strong 111
                1 (1978) 61-110 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0003-4916(78)90224-5"}> doi:10.1016/0003-4916(78)90224-5
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li#BayenFlatoFronsdalLichnerowiczSternheimer78b
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fran%C3%A7ois+Bayen"}> François Bayen
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mosh%C3%A9+Flato"} Moshé Flato
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christian+Fronsdal"} Christian Fronsdal
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andr%C3%A9+Lichnerowicz"} André Lichnerowicz
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Sternheimer"} Daniel Sternheimer
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Deformation theory and quantization. II. Physical applications
                %strong 111
                1 (1978) 111-151 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0003-4916(78)90225-7"}> doi:10.1016/0003-4916(78)90225-7
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p Review:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alan+Weinstein"}> Alan Weinstein
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Deformation quantization
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/item/?id=SB_1993-1994__36__389_0"} numdam:SB_1993-1994__36__389_0
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Sternheimer"}> Daniel Sternheimer
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Deformation Quantization: Twenty Years After
                %strong 453
                (1998) 107-145 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/9809056"}> arXiv:math/9809056
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                Nima Moshayedi:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Kontsevich’s Deformation Quantization and Quantum Field Theory
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-031-05122-7"} doi:10.1007/978-3-031-05122-7
              %blockquote
                %p
                  (relating also to the
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+sigma-model"} Poisson sigma-model
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li#Gutt83
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Simone+Gutt"}> Simone Gutt
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    An explicit
                    = succeed "-product" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mo *
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ast
                %strong 7
                (1983) 249–258 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BF00400441"}> doi:10.1007/BF00400441
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li#Gutt11
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Simone+Gutt"}> Simone Gutt
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Deformation quantization of Poisson manifolds
                %strong 17
                (2011) 171-220 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://msp.org/gtm/2011/17/p003.xhtml"}> gtm:17
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://msp.org/gtm/2011/17/gtm-2011-17-003p.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0003107"} arXiv:math/0003107
          %p Monographs:
          %ul
            %li#Waldmann07
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stefan+Waldmann"}> Stefan Waldmann
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Poisson-Geometrie und Deformationsquantisierung
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-540-72518-3"} doi:10.1007/978-3-540-72518-3
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fedosov+deformation+quantization"} Fedosov deformation quantization
            prescription for deformation quantization of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+manifolds"} symplectic manifolds
            and varieties and also of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+manifolds"} Poisson manifolds
            that have a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+foliation"} regular foliation
            by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+leaves"} symplectic leaves
            is discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Boris+Fedosov"}> Boris Fedosov
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Formal quantization
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Boris+Fedosov"}> Boris Fedosov
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Index theorem in the algebra of quantum observables
            %li#Fedosov94
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Boris+Fedosov"}> Boris Fedosov
                ,
                %em A simple geometrical construction of deformation quantization
                J. Differential Geom. Volume 40, Number 2 (1994), 213-238. (
                %a{:href => "http://projecteuclid.org/euclid.jdg/1214455536"}> EUCLID
                )
          %p For algebraic forms this is discussed in
          %ul
            %li#BK09
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Roman+Bezrukavnikov"}> Roman Bezrukavnikov
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dmitry+Kaledin"} Dmitry Kaledin
              %em Fedosov quantization in algebraic context
              Mosc. Math. J., Volume 4, Number 3, (2004) 559–592 (
              %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/distribution/mmj/vol4-3-2004/bezrukavnikov-kaledin.pdf"}> AMS pdf
              )
          %p More discussion of this approach is in
          %ul
            %li
              Claudio Emmrich,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alan+Weinstein"} Alan Weinstein
              %em The differential geometry of Fedosov’s quantization
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9311094"}> arXiv:hep-th/9311094
              )
          %p A direct and general formula for the deformation quantization of any Poisson manifold was given in
          %ul
            %li#Kontsevich97
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Maxim+Kontsevich"}> Maxim Kontsevich
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Deformation quantization of Poisson manifolds
              %strong 66
              (2003), no. 3, 157–216, (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/q-alg/9709040"}> arXiv:q-alg/9709040
              ).
          %p see also
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Peter Banks, Erik Panzer, Brent Pym,
                %em Multiple zeta values in deformation quantization
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1812.11649"}> arXiv:1812.11649
                )
            %li
              %p
                Kelvin Ritland:
                %em Deformation quantization generates all multiple zeta values
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2409.18450"}> arXiv:2409.18450
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            This secretly uses the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+sigma-model"} Poisson sigma-model
            (see there for more details) induced by the given target
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+Lie+algebroid"} Poisson Lie algebroid
          %p
            A popular exposition of formal deformation quantization with emphasis of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} stringy
            = succeed "-construction:" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+sigma-model"} Poisson sigma-model
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Anton+Kapustin"}> Anton Kapustin
              ,
              %em Quantum geometry: The reunion of math and physics
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Kapustin-QuantumGeometry.pdf", :title => "pdf"}> pdf
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p The classification of the space of such formal deformation quantization is discussed in
          %ul
            %li#Dolgushev1109
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vasily+Dolgushev"}> Vasily Dolgushev
                ,
                %em Stable Formality Quasi-isomorphisms for Hochschild Cochains I
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1109.6031"}> arXiv:1109.6031
                )
            %li#Dolgushev1111
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vasily+Dolgushev"}> Vasily Dolgushev
                ,
                %em Exhausting formal quantization procedures
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1111.2797"}> arXiv:1111.2797
                )
            %li#DolgushevRogersWillwacher12
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vasily+Dolgushev"}> Vasily Dolgushev
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christopher+Rogers"} Christopher Rogers
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas+Willwacher"} Thomas Willwacher
                %em Kontsevich’s graph complex, GRT, and the deformation complex of the sheaf of polyvector fields
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1211.4230"}> arXiv:1211.4230
                )
          %p
            Deformation quantization of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polynomial+Poisson+algebras"} polynomial Poisson algebras
            via
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+enveloping+algebra"} universal enveloping algebra
            (generalizing that of
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie-Poisson+structures"} Lie-Poisson structures
          %ul
            %li#PenkavaVanhaecke00
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Penkava"}> Michael Penkava
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pol+Vanhaecke"} Pol Vanhaecke
              = succeed "," do
                %em Deformation Quantization of Polynomial Poisson Algebras
              %strong 227
              1 (2000) 365-393 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/9804022"}> arXiv:math/9804022
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1006/jabr.1999.8239"} doi:10.1006/jabr.1999.8239
          %p Deformation quantization of algebraic varieties is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Amnon+Yekutieli"}> Amnon Yekutieli
              , Deformation Quantization in Algebraic Geometry, Advances in Mathematics
              %strong 198
              (2005) 383-432.
              %p
                Erratum: Advances in Mathematics
                %strong 217
                (2008) 2897-2906.
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li
              MO discussion ,
              %em
                %a{:href => "http://mathoverflow.net/questions/42148/kontsevichs-conjectures-on-the-grothendieck-teichmuller-group"} Kontsevich’s conjectures on the Grothendieck-Teichmüller group?
          %p
            Deformation quantization in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbative+quantum+field+theory"} perturbative quantum field theory
            is discussed for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+field+theory"} free field theory
            is due to
          %ul
            %li#Dito90
              Joseph Dito,
              = succeed "." do
                %em Star-product approach to quantum field theory: The free scalar field
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://inspirehep.net/record/303898/"} spire
          %p and further expanded on in
          %ul
            %li#DuetschFredenhagen00
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+D%C3%BCtsch"}> Michael Dütsch
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Klaus+Fredenhagen"} Klaus Fredenhagen
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Algebraic Quantum Field Theory, Perturbation Theory, and the Loop Expansion
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0001129"} arXiv:hep-th/0001129
            %li#DuetschFredenhagen01
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+D%C3%BCtsch"}> Michael Dütsch
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Klaus+Fredenhagen"} Klaus Fredenhagen
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Perturbative algebraic quantum field theory and deformation quantization
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://xxx.uni-augsburg.de/abs/hep-th/0101079"} arXiv:hep-th/0101079
            %li#HirschfeldHenselder02
              %p
                A. C. Hirshfeld, P. Henselder,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Star Products and Perturbative Quantum Field Theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0208194"} arXiv:hep-th/0208194
          %p
            and for interacting
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbative+quantum+field+theory"} perturbative quantum field theory
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbative+AQFT"}> perturbative AQFT
            ) in
          %ul
            %li#Collini16
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Giovanni+Collini"}> Giovanni Collini
                ,
                %em Fedosov Quantization and Perturbative Quantum Field Theory
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1603.09626"}> arXiv:1603.09626
                )
            %li#HawkinsRejzner16
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eli+Hawkins"}> Eli Hawkins
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kasia+Rejzner"} Kasia Rejzner
                %em The Star Product in Interacting Quantum Field Theory
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1612.09157"}> arXiv:1612.09157
                )
          %p
            The relation to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+quantization"} geometric quantization
            is discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eli+Hawkins"}> Eli Hawkins
                ,
                %em The Correspondence between Geometric Quantization and Formal Deformation Quantization
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/9811049"}> arXiv:math/9811049
                )
            %li
              %p
                Christoph Nölle,
                %em Geometric and deformation quantization
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0903.5336"}> arXiv:0903.5336
                )
          %p and some remarks on the relation are also in section 1.4 of
          %ul
            %li#GukovWitten09
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sergei+Gukov"}> Sergei Gukov
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"} Edward Witten
              = succeed "," do
                %em Branes and Quantization
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0809.0305"} arXiv:0809.0305
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://projecteuclid.org/euclid.atmp/1282054099"} euclid
          %p
            which is about
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantization+via+the+A-model"} quantization via the A-model
          %p
            The formulation of deformation quantization as lifts from
            %span.newWikiWord
              P-n operads
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/P-n+operads"} ?
            over
            %span.newWikiWord
              BD-n operads
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/BD-n+operads"} ?
            to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-n+operads"} E-n operads
            is discussed in section 2.3 and 2.4 of
          %ul
            %li#CostelloGwilliam
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kevin+Costello"}> Kevin Costello
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Owen+Gwilliam"} Owen Gwilliam
              %em Factorization algebras in perturbative quantum field theory
              (
              %a{:href => "http://math.northwestern.edu/~costello/factorization_public.html"}> wiki
              , early/partial draft
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://math.northwestern.edu/~gwilliam/factorization.pdf"} pdf
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Weyl_quantization#Deformation_quantization"} Wikipedia
            %li
              %p
                F. Bayen, M. Flato, C. Fronsdal, A. Lichnerowicz, D. Sternheimer,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Quantum mechanics as a deformation of classical mechanics
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=674337"} MR674337
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.1007/BF00399745"} doi
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Deformation theory and quantization. I. Deformations of symplectic structures
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=496157"} MR496157
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Deformation theory and quantization. II. Physical applications
                %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=496158"} MR496158
            %li
              %p
                M. Flato, A. Lichnerowicz, D. Sternheimer,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Deformations of Poisson brackets, Dirac brackets and applications
                %strong 17
                (1976), no. 9, 1754–1762,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=420723"} MR420723
                %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.1063/1.523104"} doi
            %li
              %p
                D. Arnal, J.-C. Cortet,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo *
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ast
                    \-products in the method of orbits for nilpotent groups
                %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.1016/0393-0440(85)90010-5"} doi
          %p
            On the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stack"} stack
            of deformation quantizations:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Maxim+Kontsevich"}> Maxim Kontsevich
                ,
                %em Deformation quantization of algebraic varieties
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0106006"}> arXiv:math/0106006
                )
            %li
              %p
                Pietro Polesello,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pierre+Schapira"} Pierre Schapira
                %em Stacks of quantization-deformation modules on complex symplectic manifolds
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0305171"}> arXiv:math/0305171
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Amnon+Yekutieli"}> Amnon Yekutieli
                ,
                %em Twisted Deformation Quantization of Algebraic Varieties
                ,
              %p
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0905.0488"} arxiv:0905.0488
          %p
            The action of a
